anty-Mansi Autonomous Okrug, a key area for the Russian oil industry, which has driven both economic growth and demographic changes in the region. The city, built primarily to support the burgeoning oil industry, reflects the intersection of natural resources and urban development in post-Soviet Russia, making it significant for understanding modern economic transformations in Eastern Europe.

